The binary is a Snap7-based client. Sizes like 100 pass but huge sizes are rejected. Let me find the validation boundary and probe for the crash.

<tool_call>
{
  "name": "Bash",
  "arguments": {
    "command": "cd /tmp && python3 -c \"\nimport struct, subprocess\n# binary search on size validation boundary\nfor size in [65535, 65536, 65534, 32768, 16384, 8192, 100000, 1000000]:\n    data = struct.pack('<ii', 0, size) + b'A'*16\n    open('/tmp/t.bin','wb').write(data)\n    r = subprocess.run(['/workspace/artifacts/target/s7dl','/tmp/t.bin'], capture_output=True, timeout=10)\n    print(f'size={size:10d} rc={r.returncode} out={r.stdout!r}')\n\"",
    "description": "Find size validation boundary"
  }
}
</tool_call>

<tool_call>
{
  "name": "Bash",
