Now let me also fix the `returncode` semantics — the contract expects the child process exit status; our forced termination produces a negative returncode which we convert. Let me also reconsider the timeout handling and add a global watchdog so `timed_out` is reported:

<tool_call>
{
  "name": "Edit",
  "arguments": {
    "replace_all": false,
    "file_path": "/workspace/out/poc.py",
    "old_string": "def run(binary_path, timeout):\n    \"\"\"Drive the interaction.  Returns (observable_value_dict, meta_dict).\"\"\"\n    started = time.time()\n    deadline = started + max(5.0, timeout - 5.0)\n",
    "new_string": "def run(binary_path, timeout):\n    \"\"\"Drive the interaction.  Returns (observable_value_dict, meta_dict).\"\"\"\n    started = time.time()\n    deadline = started + max(5.0, timeout - 5.0)"
  }
}
</tool_call>

